{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.110.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-44487-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-44487 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-44487\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.13\nFix Version: 1.20.10,1.21.3\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-44487](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-44487)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-44487**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.17.13  | 1.20.10,1.21.3  | go-module  | /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-44487](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-44487)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3-golang.org/x/net",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3 medium vulnerability for golang.org/x/net package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP/2 Stream Cancellation Attack"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nVersion: v0.8.0\nFix Version: 0.17.0\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner\nData Namespace: github:language:go\nLink: [GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | golang.org/x/net  | v0.8.0  | 0.17.0  | go-module  | /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner  | github:language:go  | [GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@v0.8.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45288-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45288 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker may cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data by sending an excessive number of CONTINUATION frames. Maintaining HPACK state requires parsing and processing all HEADERS and CONTINUATION frames on a connection. When a request's headers exceed MaxHeaderBytes, no memory is allocated to store the excess headers, but they are still parsed. This permits an attacker to cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data, all associated with a request which is going to be rejected. These headers can include Huffman-encoded data which is significantly more expensive for the receiver to decode than for an attacker to send. The fix sets a limit on the amount of excess header frames we will process before closing a connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45288\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.13\nFix Version: 1.21.9,1.22.2\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-45288](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45288**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.17.13  | 1.21.9,1.22.2  | go-module  | /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-45288](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
