            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-24534-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-24534 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP and MIME header parsing can allocate large amounts of memory, even when parsing small inputs, potentially leading to a denial of service. Certain unusual patterns of input data can cause the common function used to parse HTTP and MIME headers to allocate substantially more memory than required to hold the parsed headers. An attacker can exploit this behavior to cause an HTTP server to allocate large amounts of memory from a small request, potentially leading to memory exhaustion and a denial of service. With fix, header parsing now correctly allocates only the memory required to hold parsed headers."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-24534\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.13\nFix Version: 1.19.8,1.20.3\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-24534](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-24534)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-24534**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.17.13  | 1.19.8,1.20.3  | go-module  | /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-24534](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-24534)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22871-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22871 critical vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/http package improperly accepts a bare LF as a line terminator in chunked data chunk-size lines. This can permit request smuggling if a net/http server is used in conjunction with a server that incorrectly accepts a bare LF as part of a chunk-ext."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22871\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.13\nFix Version: 1.23.8,1.24.2\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/local-path-provisioner\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-22871](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-22871)",
